<urn:beads-cache:finding:CI-C4-001> triage:id "CI-C4-001" ; triage:sprint "c-3" ; triage:originSprint "c-4" ; triage:severity "important" ; triage:location "scripts/runtime_templates.py:200" ; triage:source "independent flaky-test-qa /tmp/phase-c-local-cleanup-review-result.md" ; triage:status "closed" ; triage:record "{\"evidence\": \"At scripts/runtime_templates.py:181 timeout handling calls stop_tree(); :183 then completes bounded communicate(), and :191 raises the diagnostic timeout error. finally at :200 calls stop_tree() again; its :167 os.killpg(process.pid, SIGKILL) has no idempotence guard. /tmp/phase-c-current-ci-125704245410.log:415-417 shows TEMPLATE.UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT with exit_status=-9, stdout='parent diagnostic\\\\ndescendant ready\\\\n' and stderr='descendant diagnostic\\\\n'. Log lines 426-430 then show runtime_templates.py:200 -> :167 raising PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted, causing test_runtime_templates.py:404/:466 to error. The supplied log reports 109 tests with one error and one skip. The assigned branch and exact HEAD were verified before review.\", \"file\": \"scripts/runtime_templates.py\", \"id\": \"CI-C4-001\", \"issue\": \"POSIX timeout cleanup signals the owned process group once in the TimeoutExpired handler, reaps the direct child through bounded communicate(), and constructs TEMPLATE.UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT. The unconditional finally then signals the same process group again. stop_tree() does not record successful termination and only catches ProcessLookupError, so its second killpg can raise PermissionError as the group is being torn down on macOS. This replaces the expected structured timeout error and aborts the remaining finally cleanup. The supplied CI log demonstrates this exact local-tooling failure after successful timeout termination; it is not a stalled upstream renderer or a deficient timeout duration.\", \"line\": 200, \"mechanism\": \"parallel_race\", \"recommendation\": \"Make process-tree termination idempotent using explicit state that records the first successful group termination request (or established absence), so finally does not signal that group again after successful timeout cleanup. Preserve the first cleanup attempt even when the direct child already exited, since descendants may remain. Retain bounded child reaping and pipe cleanup on every path, and surface a genuine initial termination/permission failure as a structured cleanup failure instead of suppressing it. Add deterministic coverage that asserts one group termination after timeout and that an initial PermissionError is not silently accepted; retain both existing ready-descendant scenarios. Do not widen timeouts, retry killpg or broadly swallow PermissionError.\", \"severity\": \"important\", \"test\": \"ProcessDeadlineTest.test_timeout_after_descendant_ready_terminates_tree_and_preserves_diagnostics\"}" .

<urn:beads-cache:finding:CI-C4-001> triage:developerStatus "implemented_pending_qa3" ; triage:developerEvidence "Single owned termination lifecycle; repeated-cleanup PermissionError regression, first-failure propagation and resource closure, Windows Job lifecycle assertion. Parent owns independent QA and closure." .

